Subject: Recognise a class declared only by an elaborated type specifier

`struct b f();` declares `b` as well as `f`: where nothing else in the header
mentions `b`, the elaborated type specifier in the return type is the only
declaration it ever gets, and it is an incomplete type. bindgen emits it as
`#[derive(Default)] pub struct b { pub _address: u8 }`, which is what it writes
for an empty class that has a definition, where a class declared on a line of
its own comes out `pub struct b { _unused: [u8; 0] }`. Nothing downstream can
tell the first from `struct b {};`, so autocxx goes on to write C++ which
allocates, moves and destroys a `b`, none of which compiles.

`CompInfo::from_ty` decides `is_forward_declaration` from the cursor which led
it to the type rather than from the type. A declaration cursor is asked whether
it is the definition, a parameter is assumed to name something undefined, and
every other kind - the function or method whose return type it is, a field, a
variable, a typedef - is assumed to name something defined. That last guess is
the one which is wrong here.

For those other kinds, ask the type's own declaration whether clang has a
definition for it anywhere in the translation unit. A class defined further
down the header has one and is unaffected; the two existing arms are left as
they are.

--- a/ir/comp.rs
+++ b/ir/comp.rs
@@ -1730,7 +1730,17 @@
                 CXCursor_ParmDecl => true,
                 CXCursor_StructDecl | CXCursor_UnionDecl |
                 CXCursor_ClassDecl => !cur.is_definition(),
-                _ => false,
+                // Any other cursor is a use of the type, not a declaration of
+                // it, so its kind says nothing either way: the definition may
+                // be elsewhere in the header, or nowhere. Ask the declaration.
+                _ => {
+                    matches!(
+                        cursor.kind(),
+                        CXCursor_StructDecl |
+                            CXCursor_UnionDecl |
+                            CXCursor_ClassDecl
+                    ) && cursor.definition().is_none()
+                }
             });
 
         let mut maybe_anonymous_struct_field = None;
